        {
          "id": "Measure C2026",
          "title": "City of Santa Maria General Services",
          "summary": "Adds a one-half cent local sales (transactions and use) tax in the City of Santa Maria, on top of the existing one-cent Measure U tax, until ended by voters. It is a general tax; the City estimates about $13,000,000 a year for general city services such as parks and recreation, the aquatic center, library, youth programs, and roads and streets, with annual independent audits reviewed by the City Council.",
          "yesMeans": "Santa Maria adds a one-half cent sales tax for general city services until voters end it.",
          "noMeans": "The additional one-half cent sales tax is not adopted.",
